    <briefdescription>
<para>Minimal in-memory mock of ITransactionCoordinator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Records method invocations and models a simple state machine so that the interface contract tests can assert on real state transitions.</para>
<para>This mock represents a configurable 2PC coordinator for most tests; its protocol flags can be overridden to simulate other protocols.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="note"><para>Not thread-safe — designed for single-threaded unit tests only. The ITransactionCoordinator interface requires thread safety; production implementations must add synchronisation. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
